# Netlify publish-directory headers (https://docs.netlify.com/routing/headers/).
# Copied into dist/ by build.sh, so it travels WITH the deployed files.
#
# Why this exists alongside the [[headers]] block in netlify.toml: the toml
# rule for "/*" was not being applied on the live deploy even though the
# per-path CORS rules in the same file were. _headers is the file-based form
# Netlify reads straight from the publish dir and is the more robust of the two.
#
#   X-Frame-Options SAMEORIGIN  -> admin portal / builder cannot be framed by
#                                  another site (clickjacking). SAMEORIGIN, not
#                                  DENY, so future self-embedding still works.
#   X-Content-Type-Options      -> no MIME sniffing.
#   Referrer-Policy             -> origin only on cross-origin requests, so the
#                                  ?session= query in builder URLs never reaches
#                                  Google Fonts in a Referer.
/*
  X-Frame-Options: SAMEORIGIN
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
